    <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="class_t_t_y" kindref="compound">TTY</ref> reader thread implementation — shared across all platform backends. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This file contains only <ref refid="class_t_t_y_1a5069e6a70b48c9e44fef6d6fd8fa2b31" kindref="member">TTY::run()</ref>, the reader thread loop that is common to all platform implementations. Platform-specific code lives in <ref refid="_unix_t_t_y_8cpp" kindref="compound">UnixTTY.cpp</ref> and <ref refid="_windows_t_t_y_8cpp" kindref="compound">WindowsTTY.cpp</ref>.</para>
<sect1 id="_t_t_y_8cpp_1autotoc_md67_1s1"><sect2 id="_t_t_y_8cpp_1autotoc_md67_1s2"><sect3 id="_t_t_y_8cpp_1autotoc_md67">
<title>Reader thread lifecycle</title><para><orderedlist>
<listitem><para><ref refid="classThread" kindref="compound" external="/Users/jreng/Documents/Poems/JUCE/docs/doxygen/doc/juce.tag">Thread</ref> starts inside the platform <computeroutput>open()</computeroutput> call via <computeroutput>startThread()</computeroutput>.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>run()</computeroutput> sets thread priority to high and enters the main poll loop.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Each iteration blocks on <computeroutput>waitForData</computeroutput>.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>When data arrives the inner drain loop calls <computeroutput>read()</computeroutput> until no bytes remain, firing <computeroutput>events.get(id::data, chunk, n)</computeroutput> for each chunk.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>After a full drain <computeroutput>events.get(id::drainComplete)</computeroutput> is fired once.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>On EOF (<computeroutput>read()</computeroutput> returns -1) <computeroutput>events.get(id::shellExited)</computeroutput> is fired and the thread returns.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><ref refid="classThread" kindref="compound" external="/Users/jreng/Documents/Poems/JUCE/docs/doxygen/doc/juce.tag">Thread</ref> stops when <computeroutput>threadShouldExit()</computeroutput> becomes true (set by <computeroutput>close()</computeroutput>).</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="class_t_t_y_1a5069e6a70b48c9e44fef6d6fd8fa2b31" kindref="member">TTY::run()</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="class_unix_t_t_y" kindref="compound">UnixTTY</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para>WindowsTTY </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
</sect3></sect2></sect1>
    </detaileddescription>
